### PayVerse — auth-service through the gateway (environment "local").
# The OTP is printed by the MOCK LogOtpSender: run `make otp` (or check the auth-service log).

### 1. Request a login OTP (sign-up and login are the same flow). Limit: 3 per 10 min per mobile, 5/min per IP.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}" }

### 2. Verify the OTP → tokens. Replace the otp value with the one from `make otp`.
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}", "otp": "123456", "deviceId": "http-client-device-01", "deviceName": "IntelliJ HTTP Client" }

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 3. Who am I
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Rotate the refresh token (presenting an old one again revokes the session family)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/token/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}", "deviceId": "http-client-device-01" }

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### 5. Set the transaction PIN (4 or 6 digits; weak PINs like 1234 / 0000 are rejected)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/pin
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pin": "4826" }

### 6. Change the PIN
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/pin/change
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPin": "4826", "newPin": "739104" }

### 7. Forgot PIN: request a reset OTP (always 202)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/pin/reset/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}" }

### 8. Reset the PIN with the OTP from `make otp`
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/pin/reset/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}", "otp": "123456", "newPin": "582039" }

### 9. Bound devices
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/devices
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 10. Revoke a device (ends its sessions)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/devices/some-other-device-id
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 11. Logout
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### --- Direct calls to auth-service (port 8081): not routed by the gateway ---

### JWKS (public keys used by the gateway and every service)
GET {{auth}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### Service token (client_credentials). The secret is SERVICE_CLIENT_SECRET in .env.
POST {{auth}}/api/v1/auth/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=transaction-service&client_secret={{serviceClientSecret}}

> {% client.global.set("serviceToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Internal: verify a PIN (role SERVICE)
POST {{auth}}/internal/auth/pin/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{serviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "pin": "4826" }

### Internal: resolve a mobile number to a user
POST {{auth}}/internal/auth/users/lookup
Authorization: Bearer {{serviceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}" }
